{"text": "Seven O'Clock.\n\nEvery morning at seven, a stranger sent Mateo the sea.\n\nIt started on the first Monday of the summer. Mateo was in bed. His phone made a small sound.\n\nThere was a photo from a number he didn't know. The water was green and blue, and the sky was pink.\n\nUnder the photo, there was a message. \"Good morning, little sister! Look, the sea is quiet today.\"\n\nMateo read it twice. He was fifteen, and he was a boy. He had no sister.\n\nSo who was this person?\n\nMateo lived on a small island in the Atlantic. His house was yellow, with a blue balcony. From the balcony, he could see the beach.\n\nUsually, Mateo spent every summer in the water. But this summer was different. Three days before, he fell off his bike. Now his broken leg was in a heavy white cast.\n\n\"Six weeks,\" the doctor said. \"No swimming, no football, no beach.\"\n\nSix weeks! That was the whole summer!\n\nHis friends were away, too. Rui was with his grandparents, and Leo was at a camp. Mateo was alone in his room with his leg.\n\nOn the first day, Mateo watched TV. On the third day, he looked at the wall.\n\n\"I'm so boring,\" he told his mum.\n\nMum laughed. \"No, you're bored. Boring is different.\"\n\nShe sat on his bed. \"Show me that photo again. The one from the stranger.\"\n\nMateo showed her. He always told his mum about strange messages. It was a family rule.\n\n\"It's our beach,\" said Mum. \"Look, there are the black rocks.\"\n\n\"Should I answer?\" asked Mateo.\n\n\"Not yet,\" said Mum. \"Never send photos of yourself. Never give our address. And always show me first.\"\n\nThe photos came every morning at seven. On Tuesday, there was a white bird on the water. On Wednesday, there were small fishing boats.\n\nEvery message started with the same words. \"Good morning, little sister!\"\n\nMateo often thought about his first swimming lesson. He was six. A tall woman with a red hat taught him. She had a whistle and a kind laugh.\n\n\"Head up, Mateo!\" she shouted. \"Kick your legs!\"\n\nHe was afraid of the waves, but she was never angry.\n\nOn Friday, Mateo woke up at seven. He looked at his phone.\n\nNothing.\n\nAt eight, there was still no photo. At nine, there was nothing again. Why did the photos stop?", "textSha256": "771926415c54ab40fc92c7afe9591de89f52285757f6925b1db76ec727e82edf", "voice_id": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "speed": 0.95, "lang": "en", "parts": 1, "alignment": {"characters": ["S", "e", "v", "e", "n", " ", "O", "'", "C", "l", "o", "c", "k", ".", "\n", "\n", "E", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "m", "o", "r", "n", "i", "n", "g", " ", "a", "t", " ", "s", "e", "v", "e", "n", ",", " ", "a", " ", "s", "t", "r", "a", "n", "g", "e", "r", " ", "s", "e", "n", "t", " ", "M", "a", "t", "e", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "e", "a", ".", "\n", "\n", "I", "t", " ", "s", "t", "a", "r", "t", "e", "d", " ", "o", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "i", "r", "s", "t", " ", "M", "o", "n", "d", "a", "y", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "u", "m", "m", "e", "r", ".", " ", "M", "a", "t", "e", "o", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "i", "n", " ", "b", "e", "d", ".", " ", "H", "i", "s", " ", "p", "h", "o", "n", "e", " ", "m", "a", "d", "e", " ", "a", " ", "s", "m", "a", "l", "l", " ", "s", "o", "u", "n", "d", ".", "\n", "\n", "T", "h", "e", "r", "e", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "a", " ", "p", "h", "o", "t", "o", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "a", " ", "n", "u", "m", "b", "e", "r", " ", "h", "e", " ", "d", "i", "d", "n", "'", "t", " ", "k", "n", "o", "w", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "w", "a", "t", "e", "r", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "g", "r", "e", "e", "n", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "b", "l", "u", "e", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "k", "y", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "p", "i", "n", "k", ".", "\n", "\n", "U", "n", "d", "e", "r", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "p", "h", "o", "t", "o", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", "r", "e", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "a", " ", "m", "e", "s", "s", "a", "g", "e", ".", " ",